0..75 Comment "// Copy-on-write pays for a holder count it reads at every write, even when"
76..154 Comment "// the string is held once. A write that reads no count is sound exactly where"
155..234 Comment "// the string has one holder: there it writes what copy-on-write writes, and on"
235..314 Comment "// a shared string it would write the buffer another string reads. So where the"
315..391 Comment "// program states that a string is not copied for a scope, the count and its"
392..471 Comment "// branch can go (Racordon et al., \"Implementation strategies for mutable value"
472..530 Comment "// semantics\", _Journal of Object Technology_ 21(2), 2022,"
531..610 Comment "// doi:10.5381/jot.2022.21.2.a2, § 4: uniqueness-elided copies). The statement"
611..691 Comment "// is a grade on the string: `hold[1] s = e;` holds a string made where the hold"
692..771 Comment "// stands, which nothing else holds while it is held, and the checker refuses a"
772..849 Comment "// grade-one hold of a string that may have been copied. The items below show"
850..895 Comment "// the write the grade licenses, and on what."
897..972 Comment "// The lists; the byte lists; the owned bytes; where they live; the writes."
